    "result_text": "`AcceptanceTest` is the only test class, and the full build passes. Done.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the `bulkSignupWarning` flag following the exact precedent already used for the other derived, collection-dependent owner fields (`namesakeCount`, `customerCode`): a `@Transient` field on `Owner` that the create controller populates and the mapper auto-maps into the DTO.\n\nChanges:\n1. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 added a `bulkSignupWarning` boolean (readOnly) property to the `Owner` schema, so the generated `OwnerDto` exposes it.\n2. **`BulkSignupWarning.java`** (new) \u2014 a small, self-contained helper mirroring `DailyRegistrationLimit`: `isTriggered(...)` returns true when more than 80 owners already share today's registration date.\n3. **`Owner.java`** \u2014 added a `@Transient bulkSignupWarning` field with getter/setter (MapStruct auto-maps it to the DTO by name, so no mapper change was needed).\n4. **`OwnerRestControllerV1.addOwner`** \u2014 one line, next to the existing `setNamesakeCount`/`setCustomerCode` assignments, setting the flag from the already-fetched `owners` collection.\n\nStructural impact was kept low: the threshold logic lives in a new cohesive class with no surrounding complexity, the mapper (which auto-maps by name) was untouched, and the only edit to the large controller class is a single added line inside one method \u2014 no method or class was grown in complexity.\n\nThe suite (`AcceptanceTest`) is green.",
